@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Terms and Conditions";
}

<div class="mb-4">
    <h1 class="h3 fw-bold mb-1">Terms and Conditions</h1>
    <p class="text-secondary small">Last updated: November 2026</p>
</div>

<div class="panel-civic">
    <div class="panel-civic-body">
        <h5 class="fw-bold mb-2">1. Acceptance of Terms</h5>
        <p class="small text-secondary mb-3">
            By accessing or submitting requests through the EcoSanitize portal, users and municipal facility operators agree to comply with these terms, local public health guidelines, and waste segregation regulations.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mb-2">2. Mandatory Waste Segregation</h5>
        <p class="small text-secondary mb-3">
            All submitted waste must be pre-sorted into designated streams: Organic, Recyclable, Hazardous, or Sanitary. Mixing hazardous chemicals, spent batteries, or biohazard disposables into general municipal waste streams is strictly prohibited under municipal environmental safety bylaws.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mb-2">3. Accurate Reporting</h5>
        <p class="small text-secondary mb-3">
            Users logging collection requests must provide accurate collection addresses, realistic weight estimates, and clear notice of any hazardous or corrosive materials. False or misleading descriptions may result in refusal of service or municipal fines.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mb-2">4. Sanitization Audit Compliance</h5>
        <p class="small text-secondary mb-3">
            Facilities receiving a cleanliness rating of 2 or below must undergo corrective deep cleaning within 48 hours of inspection. Re-inspection by an authorized municipal inspector will be scheduled automatically.
        </p>

        <h5 class="fw-bold mb-2">5. System Availability and Modifications</h5>
        <p class="small text-secondary mb-0">
            Municipal operations management reserves the right to modify collection schedules, prioritize emergency requests, and update operating procedures in response to public health emergencies or extreme weather events.
        </p>
    </div>
</div>
